Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,In the US, calling your friend's mom by her first name is normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.60,0:00:10.88,Default,,0,0,0,,In China, many people would use a kinship word instead — like "auntie" — even if
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.88,0:00:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,she's not a relative.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.62,0:00:15.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not about being formal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.00,0:00:18.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It's about marking the relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.41,0:00:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,In the US, you open a gift right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.02,0:00:24.30,Default,,0,0,0,,It shows you're excited.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.65,0:00:30.58,Default,,0,0,0,,In many Chinese homes, it can feel more polite to thank the person first — and open
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.58,0:00:31.22,Default,,0,0,0,,it later.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.57,0:00:35.25,Default,,0,0,0,,In the US, leaving a tip is expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.60,0:00:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,In China, most restaurants don't expect one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.63,0:00:42.93,Default,,0,0,0,,The menu price is usually the price.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.28,0:00:45.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Different rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.11,0:00:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Same everyday moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.86,0:00:50.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Which one would surprise you most?
